>
  <section class="section wrap service-page__intro">
    <p class="type-label service-page__eyebrow">Services</p>
    <h1 class="type-display service-page__heading">Pillows, Cushions &amp; Soft Furnishings</h1>
    <p class="service-page__lead">
      Custom pillows and cushions in Cincinnati and Northern Kentucky, the layer that finishes a
      room. These are the smallest things Amy makes and often the ones that decide whether a room
      reads as considered or merely furnished.
    </p>
  </section>

  <RevealImage
    src={leadImage}
    alt="Banded roman shade and pleated drapery framing French doors, with a crystal chandelier overhead"
    blurDataURL="data:image/webp;base64,UklGRqwAAABXRUJQVlA4IKAAAAAwBQCdASoYABUAPu1orlCppaQiqAqpMB2JZwAG0KCFeA8GvwPjvP6bHUT+YIQzyU7j0AD+FSHDV0ubeTAPHbf5413BYJW3pLc2ZHNK0MCBuh5vMwaNlvdw15DG9e1iBJcqwHR2FKUtXrkLqItBnK/DhKwBxjlP+OnZmgp6tjAHPHdy98FzAZDZkNeAJofae+wgRZ+DQT6E0ZUr/QTv/QAA"
    aspectRatio="16/9"
    sizes="100vw"
  />

  <section class="section wrap service-page__body">
    <h2 class="type-display service-page__subhead">Small work, disproportionate effect</h2>
    <p>
      A ready-made pillow is one size, one fabric, one edge, all decided by somebody who never saw
      the sofa. Custom means the proportion suits the piece it sits on and the finish is chosen
      rather than accepted. It is also the easiest way to get a remarkable textile into a room. A
      fabric that would be impractical across a whole sofa is perfect as a pair of pillows, and a
      size that does not exist ready-made is not an obstacle when Amy is making it anyway.
    </p>
    <p>
      This is often where a project starts. A client who is not ready to commit to drapery can see
      exactly how Amy works from a set of pillows, and the room moves further than the size of the
      job suggests it should.
    </p>

    <h2 class="type-display service-page__subhead">Proportion and fill</h2>
    <p>
      Size is the thing people get wrong most. Pillows that are too small leave a sofa looking
      undressed. A mix of sizes with a deliberate relationship between them beats a matched set of
      four, and two large pillows can carry a long sofa better than four small ones ever will. Seat
      depth and back height decide what belongs there, along with whether anyone actually sits on
      it.
    </p>
    <p>
      Fill decides how a pillow behaves. Down and down-blend inserts have a hand that foam cannot
      fake, and they take the karate chop, or the casual slump that makes a room look lived in
      rather than staged. Inserts are sized larger than the cover so the pillow sits full instead
      of slack. Small detail, immediately visible.
    </p>
    <p>
      The edge sets the register. A knife edge is clean and quiet. A flange softens it and reads
      traditional. Box edge where the pillow needs to hold structure. Brush fringe and tape push it
      formal fast, and there is a line past which a pillow is wearing a costume.
    </p>

    <h2 class="type-display service-page__subhead">Cushions and the rest</h2>
    <p>
      Window seats, benches, and banquettes need cushions built to an actual measurement rather
      than trimmed down to fit. Foam density gets chosen for how long people sit there, with a
      boxed construction that holds its front edge instead of collapsing into it. Dining chair
      seats take the most abuse in the house and get built accordingly. Outdoor cushions have to
      survive weather and then dry out properly.
    </p>
    <p>
      Past pillows and cushions, soft furnishings covers table linens, bed skirts, shams,
      headboards, and the occasional piece that has no standard name and simply has to be invented
      for the space it goes in.
    </p>

    <h2 class="type-display service-page__subhead">Pieces already made</h2>
    <p>
      A few finished pillows are photographed on the
      <a href="/signature-pieces" class="link-underline">signature pieces</a> page. Any of them can
      be made again, in that fabric or in one chosen for your room.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section wrap contact-band bg-ground">
    <p class="type-display contact-band__line">Ready to start your project?</p>
    <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-solid">Schedule a Consultation</a>
  </section>
